IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcrr-core`

-- Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Regulation 2025 (Qld) -- from the seat of the INJURED WORKER (the claimant).
--
-- "What counts in my NWE? What can stand in for a medical certificate? What lump sums do my DPI, my age, my care needs
-- and my pneumoconiosis give me? Do I qualify for treatment, care and support? What general damages does my ISV give,
-- and what legal costs can I recover? Is my PTSD presumed to be a work injury?" Every question is phrased as the injured
-- worker (or, for the damages and costs questions, the claimant) would ask it, on facts that person could state. The
-- rules are in wcrr-core.l4; this module restates none.
--
-- FIGURES: QOTE for 2026-27 ($1,994.50) is built in. For a day before 1 July 2026 the person gives that year's QOTE;
-- otherwise (0), and for any day after 30 June 2027, an amount stated as a multiple of QOTE answers NOTHING.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Regulation 2025 (Qld) -- the injured worker's questions`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my QOTE for` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    `the QOTE for the financial year containing` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`

§§ `The excess period (s 15)`

@export What weekly compensation amount must be exceeded to end my excess period, the period my employer pays for (Regulation s 15, Act s 65)?
GIVEN `a day in the week of payment` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week the payment is for (ISO date, e.g. 2026-09-14); it picks the financial year's QOTE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If that day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE (Queensland ordinary time earnings) for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
      `my weekly payment of compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly payment of compensation under chapter 3, part 9 of the Act, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `a day in the week of payment` `QOTE for an earlier year` `my weekly payment of compensation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my QOTE for` `a day in the week of payment` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `q` THEN JUST (`the s 15 prescribed amount` `q` `my weekly payment of compensation`)

§§ `Normal weekly earnings (ss 105-109)`

@export Can this payment be counted in my normal weekly earnings (NWE)? TRUE: it may be; FALSE: it may not; no answer: s 106 does not deal with it
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS AN `Earnings item` @desc One of: overtime, higher duties, penalties, an allowance, any other earnings
      `it was for work my employer required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment related to work your employer required you to do
      `it was regular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment was of a regular nature
      `it would have continued but for my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would still be receiving it if you had not been injured
      `it is an excluded wages item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is one of the amounts in paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition of "wages" in schedule 6 of the Act (excluded from NWE)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this payment be counted in my NWE?` `the kind of payment` `it was for work my employer required` `it was regular` `it would have continued but for my injury` `it is an excluded wages item` MEANS
    `may it be taken into account in NWE under s 106` `the kind of payment` `it was for work my employer required` `it was regular` `it would have continued but for my injury` `it is an excluded wages item`

@export Whose earnings is my normal weekly earnings (NWE) worked out from (Regulation ss 105, 107, 109)?
GIVEN `my earnings in the 12 months before the injury cannot practicably be calculated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is impracticable to calculate your earnings in the 12 months before the injury, because of how long you had been employed or the terms of your employment
      `my employer has someone comparable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer employs someone on the same or comparable terms who does the same or comparable work
      `the insurer considers the usual calculation unfair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer considers that calculating your NWE under the Regulation would be unfair (the insurer's view)
GIVETH AN `NWE basis`
`What is my NWE worked out from?` `my earnings in the 12 months before the injury cannot practicably be calculated` `my employer has someone comparable to me` `the insurer considers the usual calculation unfair` MEANS
    `the basis of the NWE` `my earnings in the 12 months before the injury cannot practicably be calculated` `my employer has someone comparable to me` `the insurer considers the usual calculation unfair`

@export Are my earnings from all my employers counted in my normal weekly earnings (Regulation s 108)?
GIVEN `I worked for 2 or more employers at once` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when injured, you were employed under contracts of service with 2 or more employers at the same time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Are my earnings from all my employers counted?` `I worked for 2 or more employers at once` MEANS
    `earnings under all the contracts are counted (s 108)` `I worked for 2 or more employers at once`

§§ `Applying for compensation (ss 113-115)`

@export What can my declaration do in place of a medical certificate when no doctor was available (Regulation s 113)?
GIVEN `my application came with a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application for compensation, DPI assessment or dependency certificate came with a medical certificate
      `no doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist was available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no doctor, nurse practitioner or registered dentist was available to attend you to give the certificate
      `I gave a declaration in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the insurer a declaration in the approved form saying none was available and describing the injury
      `the injury is fatal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury caused, or is, the worker's death
      `a declaration was already accepted for this event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has already accepted a declaration as proof of incapacity for an injury in the same event
GIVETH A `Declaration effect`
`What does my declaration do in place of a medical certificate?` `my application came with a medical certificate` `no doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist was available` `I gave a declaration in the approved form` `the injury is fatal` `a declaration was already accepted for this event` MEANS
    `the effect of the s 113 declaration` `my application came with a medical certificate` `no doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist was available` `I gave a declaration in the approved form` `the injury is fatal` `a declaration was already accepted for this event`

@export For how many days of incapacity can my declaration be proof, instead of a medical certificate (Regulation s 113(3))? No answer: a fatal injury, where no limit is set
GIVEN `my application came with a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application came with a medical certificate
      `no doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist was available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no doctor, nurse practitioner or registered dentist was available to attend you
      `I gave a declaration in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the insurer a declaration in the approved form
      `the injury is fatal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury caused, or is, the worker's death
      `a declaration was already accepted for this event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a declaration has already been accepted as proof of incapacity for an injury in the same event
      `days of incapacity I claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of incapacity you want the declaration to prove
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`For how many days can my declaration prove my incapacity?` `my application came with a medical certificate` `no doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist was available` `I gave a declaration in the approved form` `the injury is fatal` `a declaration was already accepted for this event` `days of incapacity I claim` MEANS
    `the days of incapacity the declaration can prove` (`the effect of the s 113 declaration` `my application came with a medical certificate` `no doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist was available` `I gave a declaration in the approved form` `the injury is fatal` `a declaration was already accepted for this event`) `days of incapacity I claim`

@export Can a document from a practitioner outside Queensland stand in for my medical certificate (Regulation s 114)?
GIVEN `my application came with a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application came with a Queensland-form medical certificate
      `I was injured outside Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you sustained the injury outside Queensland
      `the document is to substantially the same effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document says substantially what the medical certificate would
      `its author has a corresponding qualification and attended me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was prepared by someone with a qualification corresponding to a doctor, nurse practitioner or registered dentist who attended you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can a practitioner's document from outside Queensland stand in for my certificate?` `my application came with a medical certificate` `I was injured outside Queensland` `the document is to substantially the same effect` `its author has a corresponding qualification and attended me` MEANS
    `the document is taken to be the certificate (s 114)` `my application came with a medical certificate` `I was injured outside Queensland` `the document is to substantially the same effect` `its author has a corresponding qualification and attended me`

@export Was the insurer's requirement that I attend a personal examination made the way the Regulation requires (s 115)?
GIVEN `I was told in a written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the requirement was made by written notice
      `the notice names the examiner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice names the registered person who will examine you
      `the examiner is a specialist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the examiner is a specialist
      `the notice states the specialty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the examiner's field of specialty
      `the notice states the day, time and place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the day, time and place of the examination
      `the examiner is employed by the insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the examiner is employed by the insurer that gave the notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was the examination requirement properly made?` `I was told in a written notice` `the notice names the examiner` `the examiner is a specialist` `the notice states the specialty` `the notice states the day, time and place` `the examiner is employed by the insurer` MEANS
    `the examination requirement is made as s 115 requires` `I was told in a written notice` `the notice names the examiner` `the examiner is a specialist` `the notice states the specialty` `the notice states the day, time and place` `the examiner is employed by the insurer`

@export By when must the examiner give the insurer the written report of my examination (Regulation s 115(4))?
GIVEN `the day of my examination` IS A DATE @desc The day you were examined (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the examiner report to the insurer?` `the day of my examination` MEANS
    `the last day for the examination report` `the day of my examination`

§§ `Lump sums for permanent impairment (ss 116-121, schedules 2-4)`

@export What lump sum compensation does my degree of permanent impairment (DPI) give me (Regulation s 117)? Unrounded; no answer without that year's QOTE
GIVEN `my DPI percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment as a percentage, e.g. 10 for 10%
      `the day of the offer` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer makes the offer (ISO date); it picks the financial year's QOTE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If the offer is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What lump sum does my DPI give me?` `my DPI percentage` `the day of the offer` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the multiple` `the Act s 140 multiple` `of` (`my QOTE for` `the day of the offer` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `msc` THEN JUST (`the s 117 lump sum for a DPI of` `my DPI percentage` `with maximum statutory compensation of` `msc`)

@export What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more (Regulation s 118, schedule 3)? No answer below 30%, for a DPI that is not a whole percentage, or without that year's QOTE
GIVEN `my DPI percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment as a whole percentage, e.g. 42
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is worked out (ISO date); it picks the financial year's QOTE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If that day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more?` `my DPI percentage` `the day` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the schedule 3 multiple of QOTE for a DPI of` `my DPI percentage`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `n` THEN `the multiple` `n` `of` (`my QOTE for` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)

@export What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care (Regulation s 121, schedule 4)? No answer for a DPI under 15%, a modified Barthel index score of 75 or more, or without that year's QOTE
GIVEN `my DPI percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment as a percentage, e.g. 55
      `my modified Barthel index score` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total score on the modified Barthel index, from the occupational therapist's assessment (0 to 100; lower means more dependent)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is worked out (ISO date); it picks the financial year's QOTE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If that day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care?` `my DPI percentage` `my modified Barthel index score` `the day` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the schedule 4 multiple of QOTE for a DPI of` `my DPI percentage` `and an MBI score of` `my modified Barthel index score`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `n` THEN `the multiple` `n` `of` (`my QOTE for` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)

@export With a terminal latent onset injury, what additional lump sum do I get for my age when I lodged my application (Regulation s 116, schedule 2)?
GIVEN `my age when I lodged` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the day you lodged your application for compensation
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is worked out (ISO date); it picks the financial year's QOTE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If that day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What additional lump sum do I get for my age at lodgement?` `my age when I lodged` `the day` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    `the multiple` (`the schedule 2 multiple of QOTE for age` `my age when I lodged`) `of` (`my QOTE for` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)

@export At most how many hours of care a week can my caring allowance be decided on (Regulation s 147, schedule 8)? No answer for a modified Barthel index score of 100
GIVEN `my modified Barthel index score` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total score on the modified Barthel index, from the occupational therapist's report (0 to 100)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`At most how many hours of care a week?` `my modified Barthel index score` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dependency range for an MBI score of` `my modified Barthel index score`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `r` THEN JUST (`the schedule 8 maximum weekly hours for` `r`)

@export At what hourly rate is my caring allowance paid (Regulation s 147(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the weekly maximum carer payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount of the maximum Commonwealth carer payment, without allowances such as rent assistance, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`At what hourly rate is my caring allowance paid?` `the weekly maximum carer payment` MEANS
    `the s 147 hourly rate` `the weekly maximum carer payment`

@export What is the most caring allowance I can be paid for a week (Regulation s 147, schedule 8)? No answer for a modified Barthel index score of 100
GIVEN `my modified Barthel index score` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total score on the modified Barthel index (0 to 100)
      `the weekly maximum carer payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount of the maximum Commonwealth carer payment, without allowances, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most caring allowance a week?` `my modified Barthel index score` `the weekly maximum carer payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dependency range for an MBI score of` `my modified Barthel index score`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `r` THEN JUST ((`the schedule 8 maximum weekly hours for` `r`) TIMES (`the s 147 hourly rate` `the weekly maximum carer payment`))

§§ `Section 193A compensation (ss 122-136, schedule 5)`
-- Only for a worker to whom Act s 193A applies (injuries in the 15 October 2013 to 31 January 2015 window, whose DPI
-- has been decided). The form should ask "Does section 193A apply to you?" before this group.

@export Am I entitled to section 193A compensation (Regulation s 126)?
GIVEN `the insurer is satisfied my employer is or would have been liable to me in damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied, on the balance of probabilities, that your employer is or would have been liable to pay you damages (the insurer's decision, or the panel's on review)
      `former s 237(1)(a)(i) stops me seeking damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot seek damages because of section 237(1)(a)(i) of the Act as in force from 15 October 2013 to 31 January 2015
      `I was asked for information and did not give it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer told you it lacked information and you did not give it within 60 business days (or a later agreed day)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to section 193A compensation?` `the insurer is satisfied my employer is or would have been liable to me in damages` `former s 237(1)(a)(i) stops me seeking damages` `I was asked for information and did not give it in time` MEANS
    `the s 193A qualifying condition is satisfied` `the insurer is satisfied my employer is or would have been liable to me in damages` `former s 237(1)(a)(i) stops me seeking damages` `I was asked for information and did not give it in time`

@export How much section 193A compensation do I get (Regulation schedule 5)? No answer for a DPI outside 1% to 5%
GIVEN `the insurer is satisfied my employer is or would have been liable to me in damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer (or the panel) is satisfied your employer is or would have been liable to pay you damages
      `former s 237(1)(a)(i) stops me seeking damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether former section 237(1)(a)(i) of the Act stops you seeking damages
      `I was asked for information and did not give it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were asked for information and did not give it in time
      `my DPI percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc Your DPI as a whole percentage; with a physical and a psychological notice from one event, the higher of the two
      `my lawyer helped me give the insurer information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you engaged a lawyer and incurred legal costs giving the insurer information under s 131
      `my lawyer and I attended a meeting with the insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your lawyer attended a meeting with the insurer under s 133, incurring legal costs
      `my lawyer helped me apply to the panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you incurred legal costs applying to the panel for a review under s 136
      `my lawyer helped me give the panel information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you incurred legal costs giving the panel information under s 136(2)(c)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much section 193A compensation do I get?` `the insurer is satisfied my employer is or would have been liable to me in damages` `former s 237(1)(a)(i) stops me seeking damages` `I was asked for information and did not give it in time` `my DPI percentage` `my lawyer helped me give the insurer information` `my lawyer and I attended a meeting with the insurer` `my lawyer helped me apply to the panel` `my lawyer helped me give the panel information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the s 193A qualifying condition is satisfied` `the insurer is satisfied my employer is or would have been liable to me in damages` `former s 237(1)(a)(i) stops me seeking damages` `I was asked for information and did not give it in time`)
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the schedule 5 DPI amount for a DPI of` `my DPI percentage`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST `amount` THEN JUST (`amount` PLUS (`the schedule 5 legal cost amount` `my lawyer helped me give the insurer information` `my lawyer and I attended a meeting with the insurer` `my lawyer helped me apply to the panel` `my lawyer helped me give the panel information`))

@export After being paid a section 193A DPI amount, what further DPI amount does a later, higher notice of assessment for a different type of injury give me (Regulation schedule 5, s 3)?
GIVEN `the DPI I was paid on` IS A NUMBER @desc The DPI percentage in the first notice of assessment, on which you were paid
      `the DPI in the later notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The DPI percentage in the later notice for a different type of injury
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What further DPI amount after a second notice?` `the DPI I was paid on` `the DPI in the later notice` MEANS
    `the further schedule 5 DPI amount after a second notice` `the DPI I was paid on` `the DPI in the later notice`

@export By when may I ask the insurer for written reasons for deciding I do not meet the section 193A qualifying condition (Regulation s 130)?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the section 193A notice (ISO date)
      `public holidays` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a weekday in the 10 business days after that day
GIVETH A DATE
`By when may I ask for reasons?` `the day I received the notice` `public holidays` MEANS
    `the day` `the s 130 business days` `business days after` `the day I received the notice` `with` `public holidays` `public holidays in between`

@export By when may I give the insurer information about the section 193A qualifying condition (Regulation s 131(2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the section 193A notice saying the insurer lacks information (ISO date)
      `public holidays` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a weekday in the 60 business days after that day
      `the insurer agreed a later day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the insurer agreed a later day
      `the agreed day` IS A DATE @desc The later day agreed (ISO date); ignored if none was agreed
GIVETH A DATE
`By when may I give the insurer information?` `the day I received the notice` `public holidays` `the insurer agreed a later day` `the agreed day` MEANS
    IF `the insurer agreed a later day` AND DATE_SERIAL `the agreed day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `sixty days on`
    THEN `the agreed day`
    ELSE `sixty days on`
    WHERE
        `sixty days on` MEANS `the day` `the s 131 business days` `business days after` `the day I received the notice` `with` `public holidays` `public holidays in between`

@export By when must the insurer decide the section 193A qualifying condition after I give it information (Regulation s 132(3))? After that day it is taken to have decided against me
GIVEN `the day the insurer received my information` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received the information you gave (ISO date)
      `I met the insurer under s 133` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you met the insurer to discuss a proposed decision
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc The day of that meeting (ISO date); ignored if there was none
      `public holidays` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a weekday in the period
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the insurer decide?` `the day the insurer received my information` `I met the insurer under s 133` `the day of the meeting` `public holidays` MEANS
    `the s 132(3) decision day` `the day the insurer received my information` `I met the insurer under s 133` `the day of the meeting` `public holidays`

@export By when may I apply to the panel to review the insurer's section 193A decision (Regulation s 136(1))?
GIVEN `the day I received the written reasons` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the insurer's written reasons, or became aware it failed to decide in time (ISO date)
      `public holidays` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a weekday in the 20 business days after that day
GIVETH A DATE
`By when may I apply to the panel?` `the day I received the written reasons` `public holidays` MEANS
    `the day` `the s 136 business days` `business days after` `the day I received the written reasons` `with` `public holidays` `public holidays in between`

§§ `Pneumoconiosis (schedules 6-7)`
-- Only for a worker with pneumoconiosis (Act chapter 3, part 3, division 5).

@export What is my pneumoconiosis score from the readings of my chest x-ray, or how many more readings are needed (Regulation schedule 6)?
GIVEN `the first reading` IS A `Chest x-ray reading` @desc The ILO category the first qualified reader recorded, e.g. "category 2/1" or "category A"
      `the second reading` IS A `Chest x-ray reading` @desc The category the second reader recorded for the same x-ray
      `the third reading` IS A `Chest x-ray reading` @desc The third reading's category, or "no such reading taken"
      `the fourth reading` IS A `Chest x-ray reading` @desc The fourth reading's category, or "no such reading taken"
      `the fifth reading` IS A `Chest x-ray reading` @desc The fifth reading's category, or "no such reading taken"
GIVETH A `Pneumoconiosis score answer`
`What is my pneumoconiosis score?` `the first reading` `the second reading` `the third reading` `the fourth reading` `the fifth reading` MEANS
    `the pneumoconiosis score from readings` `the first reading` `the second reading` `the third reading` `the fourth reading` `the fifth reading`

@export What lump sum compensation does my pneumoconiosis score give me, after any reduction for my lodgement age (Regulation schedule 7)?
GIVEN `my pneumoconiosis score` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pneumoconiosis score under schedule 6 (0, 15, 20, 25, 50, 55, 60, 75, 80, 85, 90, 95 or 100)
      `my lodgement age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when you lodged your application for compensation
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is worked out (ISO date); it picks the financial year's QOTE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If that day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What lump sum does my pneumoconiosis give me?` `my pneumoconiosis score` `my lodgement age` `the day` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the schedule 7 multiple of QOTE for a score of` `my pneumoconiosis score`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `n` THEN
        CONSIDER `the multiple` `n` `of` (`my QOTE for` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `prescribed` THEN JUST (`the schedule 7 amount after the age reduction` `prescribed` `my lodgement age`)

§§ `Treatment, care and support for a serious personal injury (ss 153-160, 173-176)`
-- Only for a worker with a serious personal injury (Act chapter 4A).

@export Does my spinal cord injury meet the eligibility criteria for treatment, care and support payments (Regulation s 153)?
GIVEN `my ASIA impairment grade` IS AN `ASIA grade` @desc Your grade on the ASIA impairment scale under the ISNCSCI: grade A, grade B, grade C, grade D, or "grade E or not graded"
      `a bladder, bowel or sexual function item scored 0` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an ISAFSCI item for bladder, bowel or sexual function scored 0
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my spinal cord injury meet the criteria?` `my ASIA impairment grade` `a bladder, bowel or sexual function item scored 0` MEANS
    `a spinal cord injury meets the s 153 criteria` `my ASIA impairment grade` `a bladder, bowel or sexual function item scored 0`

@export Does my traumatic brain injury meet the eligibility criteria for treatment, care and support payments (Regulation ss 154, 160)?
GIVEN `days of post-traumatic amnesia` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of post-traumatic amnesia, assessed on the Westmead PTA scale or another approved scale
      `hours in a coma that was not induced` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours you were in a coma as a result of the injury, not counting an induced coma
      `imaging shows a significant brain abnormality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether brain imaging shows a significant brain abnormality from the injury
      `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lowest score on a motor or cognitive item of the functional independence measure (the children's version for a child), 1 to 7
      `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FIM assessor was accredited by the Australasian Rehabilitation Outcomes Centre and approved by the insurer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my brain injury meet the criteria?` `days of post-traumatic amnesia` `hours in a coma that was not induced` `imaging shows a significant brain abnormality` `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved` MEANS
    `a traumatic brain injury meets the s 154 criteria` `days of post-traumatic amnesia` `hours in a coma that was not induced` `imaging shows a significant brain abnormality` (`the FIM shows 5 or less on a motor or cognitive item, by a s 160 assessor` `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved`)

@export Does my leg amputation meet the eligibility criterion for treatment, care and support payments (Regulation s 155)?
GIVEN `the percentage of my femur's length lost` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of the femur's length lost, from X-rays before and after or by comparison with the other femur
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my leg amputation meet the criterion?` `the percentage of my femur's length lost` MEANS
    `a leg amputation meets the s 155 criterion` `the percentage of my femur's length lost`

@export Do my amputations of more than one limb meet the eligibility criteria for treatment, care and support payments (Regulation s 156)?
GIVEN `the percentage of one tibia lost` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of the length of one tibia lost (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the other tibia lost` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of the length of the other tibia lost (0 if none)
      `arms amputated at or above the thumb and index finger knuckle` IS A NUMBER @desc How many upper limbs (0, 1 or 2) were amputated at or above the first metacarpophalangeal joint of the thumb and index finger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do my amputations meet the criteria?` `the percentage of one tibia lost` `the percentage of the other tibia lost` `arms amputated at or above the thumb and index finger knuckle` MEANS
    `multiple amputations meet the s 156 criteria` `the percentage of one tibia lost` `the percentage of the other tibia lost` `arms amputated at or above the thumb and index finger knuckle`

@export Does my full thickness burn meet the eligibility criteria for treatment, care and support payments (Regulation ss 157, 160)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `percentage of my body surface burnt` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of your total body surface area with a full thickness burn
      `both my hands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the full thickness burn is to both hands
      `my face` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is to the face
      `my genital area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is to the genital area
      `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lowest motor or cognitive item score on the functional independence measure, 1 to 7
      `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FIM assessor was AROC-accredited and approved by the insurer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my burn meet the criteria?` `my age` `percentage of my body surface burnt` `both my hands` `my face` `my genital area` `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved` MEANS
    `a full thickness burn meets the s 157 criteria` `my age` `percentage of my body surface burnt` `both my hands` `my face` `my genital area` (`the FIM shows 5 or less on a motor or cognitive item, by a s 160 assessor` `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved`)

@export Does my inhalation burn meet the eligibility criterion for treatment, care and support payments (Regulation ss 158, 160)?
GIVEN `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lowest motor or cognitive item score on the functional independence measure, 1 to 7
      `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the FIM assessor was AROC-accredited and approved by the insurer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my inhalation burn meet the criterion?` `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved` MEANS
    `an inhalation burn meets the s 158 criterion` (`the FIM shows 5 or less on a motor or cognitive item, by a s 160 assessor` `my lowest FIM motor or cognitive item score` `the FIM assessor was accredited and approved`)

@export Does my blindness caused by trauma meet the eligibility criterion for treatment, care and support payments (Regulation s 159)?
GIVEN `my better eye's corrected acuity as a decimal` IS A NUMBER @desc Corrected visual acuity of your better eye on the Snellen scale, as a decimal (6/60 is 0.1, 6/6 is 1)
      `my better eye's field of vision in degrees` IS A NUMBER @desc The arc of your better eye's field of vision around central fixation, in degrees
      `my loss is assessed as equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your visual loss is assessed as equivalent to either test (the assessor's finding)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my blindness meet the criterion?` `my better eye's corrected acuity as a decimal` `my better eye's field of vision in degrees` `my loss is assessed as equivalent` MEANS
    `blindness meets the s 159 criterion` `my better eye's corrected acuity as a decimal` `my better eye's field of vision in degrees` `my loss is assessed as equivalent`

@export Can I make a payment request for this treatment, care or support expense (Regulation s 173)?
GIVEN `a funding agreement covers the period of the expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a funding agreement with the insurer for this treatment, care or support and the expense was incurred in its period
      `the day the expense was incurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the expense was incurred (ISO date)
      `the day I make the request` IS A DATE @desc The day you make, or will make, the payment request (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Payment request answer`
`Can I make a payment request?` `a funding agreement covers the period of the expense` `the day the expense was incurred` `the day I make the request` MEANS
    `can a payment request be made` `a funding agreement covers the period of the expense` `the day the expense was incurred` `the day I make the request`

@export By when must I make a payment request for a treatment, care or support expense (Regulation s 173(3))?
GIVEN `the day the expense was incurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the expense was incurred (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I make my payment request?` `the day the expense was incurred` MEANS
    `the same day` 6 `months after` `the day the expense was incurred`

@export Must the insurer approve my payment request (Regulation s 174)? TRUE: it must; FALSE: the request lapsed; no answer: s 174(3) does not oblige it, though it may still approve
GIVEN `my request lapsed because I did not give requested information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not give information the insurer asked for by the stated or agreed day
      `the expense was in my eligibility period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the expense was incurred in your eligibility period
      `it is excluded treatment, care or support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is "excluded treatment, care or support" under the Act
      `my support plan or an approved service request specifically includes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is specifically stated in your support plan (or, with no plan, specifically approved in a service request)
      `it is otherwise an approved service for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a service that is not excluded: whether it is an approved service for you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the insurer approve my payment request?` `my request lapsed because I did not give requested information` `the expense was in my eligibility period` `it is excluded treatment, care or support` `my support plan or an approved service request specifically includes it` `it is otherwise an approved service for me` MEANS
    `must the insurer approve the payment request` `my request lapsed because I did not give requested information` `the expense was in my eligibility period` `it is excluded treatment, care or support` `my support plan or an approved service request specifically includes it` `it is otherwise an approved service for me`

@export Was I given at least 20 business days' written notice before the insurer reviewed my entitlement to treatment, care and support payments (Regulation s 176(2))?
GIVEN `the day I was given the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given written notice of the review (ISO date)
      `the day of the review` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer carries out the review (ISO date)
      `public holidays` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a weekday between the two days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was I given enough notice of the review?` `the day I was given the notice` `the day of the review` `public holidays` MEANS
    `the review notice was given in time (s 176)` `the day I was given the notice` `the day of the review` `public holidays`

§§ `A claim for damages (ss 185, 187, 189, 190, schedule 17)`
-- Only for a claimant who claims damages from the employer (Act chapter 5).

@export By when can the insurer add another person as a contributor to my damages claim (Regulation s 185)?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received my notice of claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received your notice of claim (ISO date)
      `the day the insurer identified the other person` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer identified someone else as a contributor (ISO date)
      `public holidays` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a weekday in those periods
GIVETH A DATE
`By when can the insurer add a contributor?` `the day the insurer received my notice of claim` `the day the insurer identified the other person` `public holidays` MEANS
    `the last day to add a contributor` `the day the insurer received my notice of claim` `the day the insurer identified the other person` `public holidays`

@export At what amount must general damages be assessed before damages for loss of consortium or servitium can be awarded (Regulation s 187)? No answer for an injury before 1 July 2010 or without the QOTE
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker was injured (ISO date)
      `the day of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc For an injury on or after 1 July 2020: the day damages are assessed, which picks the QOTE (ISO date)
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If the assessment day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the loss of consortium threshold?` `the day of the injury` `the day of the assessment` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    `the prescribed amount for item` (`the damages table item for` `the day of the injury`) `from` `s 187 amounts` `or` `s 187 item 10 multiple` `of` (`my QOTE for` `the day of the assessment` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)

@export Can damages for loss of consortium or loss of servitium be awarded for this injury (Act s 306M(1), Regulation s 187)?
GIVEN `the worker died of the injuries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured worker died as a result of the injuries
      `general damages assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The general damages assessed for the injured worker, before allowing for contributory negligence, in dollars
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker was injured (ISO date)
      `the day of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The day damages are assessed (ISO date)
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If the assessment day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can damages for loss of consortium be awarded?` `the worker died of the injuries` `general damages assessed` `the day of the injury` `the day of the assessment` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    IF `the worker died of the injuries`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `What is the loss of consortium threshold?` `the day of the injury` `the day of the assessment` `QOTE for an earlier year`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST `threshold` THEN JUST (`general damages assessed` AT LEAST `threshold`)

@export What general damages does my injury scale value (ISV) give (Regulation s 189, schedule 17)? No answer for an ISV that is not a whole number from 0 to 100, an injury before 1 July 2010, or without the QOTE
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you were injured (ISO date); it picks the table
      `my injury scale value` IS A NUMBER @desc The injury scale value the court assesses, a whole number from 0 to 100
      `the day of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc For an injury on or after 1 July 2020: the day damages are assessed, which picks the QOTE (ISO date)
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If the assessment day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What general damages does my ISV give?` `the day of my injury` `my injury scale value` `the day of the assessment` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    `the general damages for an injury on` `the day of my injury` `with ISV` `my injury scale value` `and` (`my QOTE for` `the day of the assessment` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)

@export Above what award for future loss must the court first tell the parties its proposed terms, so a structured settlement can be negotiated (Regulation s 190, Act s 306R)?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker was injured (ISO date)
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc For an injury on or after 1 July 2020: the day the court decides the award, which picks the QOTE (ISO date)
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If that day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the structured settlement threshold?` `the day of the injury` `the day of the decision` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    `the prescribed amount for item` (`the damages table item for` `the day of the injury`) `from` `s 190 amounts` `or` `s 190 item 10 multiple` `of` (`my QOTE for` `the day of the decision` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`)

@export Must the court tell the parties the terms of its proposed award for my future loss before making it (Act s 306R(2), Regulation s 190)?
GIVEN `the proposed award for future loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The award for future loss the court proposes, not including interest, in dollars
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker was injured (ISO date)
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the court decides the award (ISO date)
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc If that day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the court first tell the parties of the proposed award?` `the proposed award for future loss` `the day of the injury` `the day of the decision` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is the structured settlement threshold?` `the day of the injury` `the day of the decision` `QOTE for an earlier year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `threshold` THEN JUST (`the proposed award for future loss` GREATER THAN `threshold`)

§§ `Legal costs of a damages claim (ss 191, 193-196, schedule 9)`
-- Only for a claimant in a damages claim or a hearing before an industrial magistrate or the industrial commission.

@export What legal costs can I recover for work done on my damages claim before a court proceeding started (Regulation ss 193-194, schedule 9)? No answer if part 9, division 2 does not apply to me
GIVEN `I am a dependant of a deceased worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim as a dependant of a worker who died
      `I have a terminal condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker with a terminal condition
      `my DPI percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment as a percentage (0 if none or not assessed)
      `the damages I recovered` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages you recovered, in dollars
      `the compensation the insurer paid me` IS A NUMBER @desc The workers' compensation the insurer paid you, in dollars
      `a compulsory conference was held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a compulsory conference was held
      `hours the conference took` IS A NUMBER @desc How long the compulsory conference took, in hours (0 if none)
      `an expert investigated liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an expert investigated liability
      `an application was made to the court before the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application was made to the court before the proceeding started
      `the court awarded legal costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court in which the proceeding was started awarded legal costs
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What pre-proceeding legal costs can I recover?` `I am a dependant of a deceased worker` `I have a terminal condition` `my DPI percentage` `the damages I recovered` `the compensation the insurer paid me` `a compulsory conference was held` `hours the conference took` `an expert investigated liability` `an application was made to the court before the proceeding` `the court awarded legal costs` MEANS
    IF NOT (`part 9, division 2 applies to the claimant` `I am a dependant of a deceased worker` `I have a terminal condition` `my DPI percentage`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the s 194 costs` (`the s 194(2) costs` `a compulsory conference was held` `hours the conference took` `an expert investigated liability` `an application was made to the court before the proceeding`) (`the damages I recovered` MINUS `the compensation the insurer paid me`) `the court awarded legal costs`)

@export How much of my liability expert's report fee is allowed as an outlay in my damages claim (Regulation s 196(1)(d), (2))?
GIVEN `the expert's fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The fee of the expert who investigated liability, in dollars
      `the insurer's agreed share of the fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The proportion of the fee the insurer agreed to pay, as a fraction (0.5 for half; 0 if none)
      `the report was disclosed before the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the report was disclosed before the court proceeding started
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my liability expert's fee is allowed?` `the expert's fee` `the insurer's agreed share of the fee` `the report was disclosed before the proceeding` MEANS
    `the allowed liability expert outlay` `the expert's fee` `the insurer's agreed share of the fee` `the report was disclosed before the proceeding`

@export How much of what my previous employers charged me for information for my notice of claim is allowed as an outlay (Regulation s 196(1)(f))?
GIVEN `each employer's fee` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The fee each previous employer charged, in dollars, one number per employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my previous employers' fees is allowed?` `each employer's fee` MEANS
    `the allowed previous employer fees` `each employer's fee`

@export At a hearing before an industrial magistrate or the industrial commission, what is the most counsel's or solicitor's costs that can be awarded (Regulation s 191)?
GIVEN `the scale C amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs under the Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999, schedule 2, part 2, scale C, in dollars
      `the magistrate or commission finds the scale inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the magistrate or commission is satisfied the scale amounts are inadequate for the work, importance, difficulty or complexity
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most counsel's or solicitor's costs that may be awarded?` `the scale C amount` `the magistrate or commission finds the scale inadequate` MEANS
    `the most counsel's or solicitor's costs that may be awarded` `the scale C amount` `the magistrate or commission finds the scale inadequate`

§§ `Post-traumatic stress disorder in first responders and eligible employees (ss 206-208, schedules 10-11)`

@export Is my occupation one prescribed for a "first responder" (Regulation s 206, schedule 10)?
GIVEN `my occupation` IS AN `Occupation` @desc Your occupation, from the schedule 10 list, or "none of these occupations"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my occupation a prescribed first responder occupation?` `my occupation` MEANS
    `is a prescribed first responder occupation` `my occupation`

@export Is my employer an entity prescribed for an "eligible employee" (Regulation s 207, schedule 11)?
GIVEN `my employing entity` IS AN `Employing entity` @desc The department you are employed by or in, from the schedule 11 list, or "none of these entities"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my employer a prescribed entity?` `my employing entity` MEANS
    `is a prescribed entity for eligible employees` `my employing entity`

@export Is my post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) taken to be a work injury for compensation (Act ss 36EB-36ED, Regulation ss 206-208)?
GIVEN `a psychiatrist diagnosed PTSD using the DSM-5 criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a psychiatrist diagnosed you with PTSD using the DSM-5 diagnostic criteria
      `I was a worker or relevant volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before the diagnosis, you were a worker or a relevant volunteer in that employment
      `my occupation` IS AN `Occupation` @desc Your occupation then, from the schedule 10 list, or "none of these occupations"
      `I had to respond to traumatic, time-critical incidents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment required you to respond to life-threatening or traumatic incidents where time may be critical
      `my employing entity` IS AN `Employing entity` @desc The department you were employed by or in, from the schedule 11 list, or "none of these entities"
      `I had repeated or extreme exposure to traumatic incidents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment required repeated or extreme exposure to the graphic details of traumatic incidents
      `it is proved my PTSD did not come from that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is proved that the PTSD did not arise out of or in that employment, or that the employment was not a significant contributing factor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my PTSD taken to be a work injury?` `a psychiatrist diagnosed PTSD using the DSM-5 criteria` `I was a worker or relevant volunteer` `my occupation` `I had to respond to traumatic, time-critical incidents` `my employing entity` `I had repeated or extreme exposure to traumatic incidents` `it is proved my PTSD did not come from that employment` MEANS
    `the PTSD is taken to be an injury (Act s 36ED)` `a psychiatrist diagnosed PTSD using the DSM-5 criteria` (`was employed as a first responder or an eligible employee` `I was a worker or relevant volunteer` `my occupation` `I had to respond to traumatic, time-critical incidents` `my employing entity` `I had repeated or extreme exposure to traumatic incidents`) `it is proved my PTSD did not come from that employment`
